; Fill a rectangle of the screen bitmap with a byte
;
; Worker of script code $81 (#R$9D81). Fills B pixel rows of C bytes with A, starting at the cell given by L (pixel
; row) and H (byte column); #R$A1DE converts the position, which is only right when L is a multiple of 8 (all scripts
; use cell-aligned rows).
; .
; Hardware: writes the screen bitmap at $4000-$57FF directly.
;
; A Byte to store
; L Pixel row of the top, a multiple of 8
; H Byte column 0-31
; C Width in bytes
; B Height in pixel rows
@label=FillBitmapRect
c$9F94 PUSH AF       ;
 $9F95 CALL $A1DE    ;
 $9F98 POP DE        ;
@label=FillBitmapRect_Row
*$9F99 PUSH HL       ;
 $9F9A PUSH BC       ;
 $9F9B LD B,C        ;
*$9F9C LD (HL),D     ;
 $9F9D INC L         ;
 $9F9E DJNZ $9F9C    ;
 $9FA0 POP BC        ;
 $9FA1 POP HL        ;
 $9FA2 CALL $9F17    ; next pixel row
 $9FA5 DJNZ $9F99    ;
 $9FA7 RET           ;
